==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-так.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ru|orv|тако}}, {{m|orv|такъ}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*tako}} (adverb), from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*takъ}} (adjective). Cognate with {{cog|uk|так}}, {{m|uk|тако}}; Belarusian {{m|be|так}}; Bulgarian {{m|bg|така}}; Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|тако}}, {{m|sh|так}}; Slovene {{m|sl|tako}}, {{m|sl|tàk}}; Czech and Polish {{m|pl|tak}}; Yiddish {{m|yi|טאַקע}}; Upper and Lower Sorbian {{m|dsb|tak}}; Lithuanian {{m|lt|tóks}}, {{m|lt|tokià}}; and Latin {{m|la|tālis}}. Akin to Old Church Slavonic pronoun {{m|cu|тъ}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ru|такъ||ru-PRO}}

====Adverb====
{{ru-adv|так}}

# {{lb|ru|with a {{lg|verb}} or [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}}}} [[like that]], [[like]] [[this]] {{gl|in that/this way, in that/this manner}} {{q|translated as "that" or "this" with some verbs}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[почему|Почему́]] [[ты]] '''так''' [[себя́]] [[ведёшь]]?|Why are you behaving '''like that'''?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[так]] [[и]] [[сказа́л]].|'''That'''<nowiki/>'s what I said.|lit=I said '''like that'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[мы|Мы]] '''так''' [[называ́ем]] [[э́ти]] [[шту́ки]].|'''That'''<nowiki/>'s what we call these things.|lit=We call these things '''like that'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[поступи́ли]] [[и́менно]] '''так'''.|They did exactly '''that'''.|lit=They acted/behaved/did things exactly '''like that'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[комнаты|Ко́мнаты]] [[расположенный|располо́жены]] '''так'''.|The rooms are situated '''like this'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[вот|Вот]] '''так''' [[была́]] [[проведённый|проведена́]] [[процеду́ра]].|This is how the procedure was conducted.|lit=The procedure was conducted '''like this'''.}}
# {{n-g|Used to indicate a high degree of something.}}
## {{sid|ru|high degree non-verb}} {{lb|ru|before a [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}} or {{lg|adverb}}}} [[so]]; ''in the negative:'' [[that]] {{gl|to a high degree}}
##: {{syn|ru|насто́лько|столь|тако́й<q:with a long-form adjective; must be declined><id:high degree>}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] '''так''' [[сло́жно]].|This is '''so''' hard.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] [[тре́бует]] [[больши́х]] [[уси́лий]], [[но]] [[э́то]] [[не]] '''так''' [[сло́жно]].|It requires a lot of effort, but it's not '''that''' difficult.}}
## {{lb|ru|before a {{lg|verb}}}} [[so]] [[much]]; ''in the negative:'' [[that]] [[much]] {{gl|to a high degree}} {{q|translated as "so" or (in the negative) "that" with some verbs that are translated with adjectives in English}}
##: {{syn|ru|насто́лько<q:less commonly>|'''так''' [[мно́го]]<q:partial>|'''так''' [[си́льно]]}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''так''' [[люблю́]] [[тебя́]].|I love you '''so much'''.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[почему|Почему́]] [[ты]] '''так''' [[зли́шься]]?|Why are you '''so''' mad?}}
# {{lb|ru|before a [[w:Content clause|content clause]] beginning with {{m|ru|что}}}} {{n-g|Used to indicate a sufficient degree of something (such that the following clause is true).}}
## {{sid|ru|sufficient degree non-verb}} {{lb|ru|before a [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}} or {{lg|adverb}}}} [[so]] {{gl|to a sufficient degree}} (''including in the negative'')
##: {{syn|ru|насто́лько|столь|тако́й<q:with a long-form adjective; must be declined><id:sufficient degree>}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] '''так''' [[сло́жно]], [[что]] [[я]] [[не]] [[могу́]] [[э́того]] [[сде́лать]].|This is '''so''' hard that I can't do it.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] [[не]] '''так''' [[сло́жно]], [[что]] [[я]] [[не]] [[могу́]] [[э́того]] [[сде́лать]].|It's not '''so''' hard that I can't do it.}}
## {{lb|ru|before a {{lg|verb}}}} [[so]] [[much]] {{gl|to a sufficient degree}} (''including in the negative'') {{q|translated as "so" with some verbs that are translated with adjectives in English}}
##: {{syn|ru|насто́лько<q:less commonly>|'''так''' [[мно́го]]<q:partial>|'''так''' [[си́льно]]}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''так''' [[люблю́]] [[тебя́]], [[что]] [[не]] [[могу́]] [[жить]] [[без]] [[тебя́]].|I love you '''so much''' that I can't live without you.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] '''так''' [[разозли́лся]], [[что]] [[швырну́л]] [[свой]] [[телефо́н]] [[на]] [[зе́млю]].|He got '''so''' angry that he smashed his phone on the floor.}}
# {{n-g|Used to refer to a previously mentioned or demonstrated degree of something.}}
## {{sid|ru|that degree non-verb}} {{lb|ru|before a [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}} or {{lg|adverb}}}} [[that]] {{gl|to that degree, to the previously mentioned or demonstrated degree}} (''including in the negative; often followed by {{m|ru|[[уж]] [[и]]}} in the negative'')
##: {{syn|ru|насто́лько|столь|тако́й<q:with a long-form adjective; must be declined><id:that degree>}}
##: {{ux|ru|— [[неужели|Неуже́ли]] [[э́то]] '''так''' [[сло́жно]] [[поня́ть]]? — [[да|Да]], [[э́то]] [[действи́тельно]] '''так''' [[сло́жно]].|— Is it really '''that''' hard to understand? — Yes, it really is '''that''' hard.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[почему|Почему́]] [[смеёшься]]? [[это|Э́то]] [[не]] '''так''' [[уж]] [[и]] [[смешно́]].|Why are you laughing? It's not '''that''' funny.}}
## {{lb|ru|before a {{lg|verb}}}} [[that]] [[much]] {{gl|to that degree, to the aforementioned degree}} (''including in the negative; often followed by {{m|ru|[[уж]] [[и]]}} in the negative'') {{q|translated as "that" with some verbs that are translated with adjectives in English}}
##: {{syn|ru|насто́лько<q:less commonly>|'''так''' [[мно́го]]<q:partial>|'''так''' [[си́льно]]}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[действи́тельно]] '''так''' [[ненави́дят]] [[нас]].|They really do hate us '''that much'''.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[не]] [[тру́сил]]. [[он|Он]] [[не]] '''так''' [[уж]] [[и]] [[боя́лся]].|He didn't chicken out. He wasn't '''''that''''' scared.}}
# {{sid|ru|same degree}} {{lb|ru|before a [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}} or {{lg|adverb}} and optionally a clause beginning with {{m|ru|как}}; often with {{m|ru|же}} to emphasise equality}} [[as]] {{gl|to the same or a similar degree}}
#: {{syn|ru|насто́лько|столь|тако́й<q:with a long-form adjective; must be declined><id:same degree>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[их|Они́]] '''так''' ([[же]]) [[краси́вы]], [[как]] [[на]] [[фотогра́фиях]].|They're '''as''' beautiful as (they are) on the photos.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[их|Их]] [[не]] '''так''' [[мно́го]], [[как]] [[ка́жется]].|There aren't '''as''' many of them as it seems.}}
# {{lb|ru|with a {{lg|verb}} or [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}} and immediately before a clause beginning with {{m|ru|что}} or {{m|ru|что́бы}}}} [[such]], [[in]] [[such]] [[a]] [[way]], [[so]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[расположенный|располо́жены]] '''так''', [[что]] [[все]] [[их]] [[мо́жно]] [[уви́деть]].|They are positioned '''such''' that they can all be seen.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[сде́лали]] '''так''', [[что́бы]] [[всё]] [[бы́ло]] [[возмо́жно]].|They made everything possible / ensured that everything would be possible.|lit=They did (things) '''in such a way''' that everything would be possible.}}
# {{lb|ru|with a {{lg|verb}} or [[short form#English:_Q4239848|short-form]] {{lg|adjective}} and immediately before a clause beginning with {{m|ru|как}}; often with {{m|ru|же}} to emphasise equality}} [[like]], [[the same]], ([[in]]) [[the]] [[same]] [[way]], [[similar]] [[to]], [[as]]
#: {{syn|ru|таки́м же о́бразом}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Она́]] [[звучи́т]] '''так''' ([[же]]), [[как]] [[в]] [[фи́льмах]].|She sounds '''the same''' as / like ((how) she does) in the films.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[расположенный|располо́жены]] '''так''' ([[же]]), [[как]] [[на]] [[схе́ме]].|They are positioned as (they are) / like ((how) they are) / '''(in) the same way''' as on the diagram.}}
# {{lb|ru|in the following construction with {{m|ru|как}} and {{m|ru|и}}}} [[and]], [[as well as]]
#: {{syn|ru|[[и]] ..., [[и]] ...}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] [[прино́сит]] [[по́льзу]] [[как]] [[молоды́м]], '''так''' [[и]] [[ста́рым]].|This benefits both the young '''and''' the old.|lit=This brings benefit '''in the same way''' (it does) to the old as (it does) to the young too.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|with a {{lg|verb}}}} ([[just]]) [[like that]] {{gl|suddenly/unexpectedly, without action, without consideration or without consequences}}
#: {{syn|ru|[[просто так|про́сто '''та́к''']]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[болезнь|Боле́знь]] [[не]] [[пройдёт]] '''так''' [[без]] [[лече́ния]].|The disease won't go away '''like that''' without treatment.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] [[тебе́]] '''так''' [[не]] [[сойдёт]] [[с]] [[рук]].|You won't get away with it '''just like that'''.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|often followed by {{m|ru|себе́}}}} [[not]] [[great]], not [[very]] [[well]], [[meh]], [[mediocre]]([[mediocrely|ly]]), [[middling]]([[middlingly|ly]]), [[so-so]]
#: {{syn|ru|посре́дственно|сре́дне|сре́дненько|[[так себе|'''та́к''' себе]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[вы́глядел]] '''та́к''' [[себе́]], [[но]] [[всё равно́]] [[появи́лся]].|He didn't look that great, but showed up anyway.}}

====Predicative====
{{head|ru|predicative}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial|often followed by {{m|ru|себе́}}}} [[not]] [[great]], [[meh]], [[mediocre]], [[middling]], [[so-so]]
#: {{syn|ru|посре́дственно|сре́дне|сре́дненько|[[так себе|'''та́к''' себе]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[по|По]] [[вку́су]] [[она́]]... [[ну|Ну]] '''так''', [[сре́дненько]].|In terms of taste... It's just kind of meh, average.}}

====Particle====
{{head|ru|particle}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[right]], [[okay]], [[yeah]] ({{n-g|while listening, indicates that one is awaiting the continuation of what is being said}})
#: {{syn|ru|ага́|tr1=ahá, agá}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[машина|Маши́на]] [[была́]] [[зелёная]]. — '''Так'''. — [[И]] [[за]] [[рулём]] [[была́]] [[же́нщина]].|The car was green. — '''Right'''. — And a woman was driving.}}
# {{lb|ru|introductory}} [[so]] ({{n-g|indicates a following explanation or example; can also replace "for example"}})
#: {{syn|ru|ита́к<q:partial>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Так''', [[наприме́р]]...|'''So''', for example...}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[климат|Кли́мат]] [[там]] [[суро́вый]], '''так''', [[моро́зы]] [[дохо́дят]] [[до]] [[сорока#Russian:_40|40]][[градусов|°]].|The climate there is harsh, '''for example''', temperatures get down to 40°C.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[nothing]] (special); [[no one]] (special); [[nowhere]] (special); [[no]] [[reason]]; etc. ({{n-g|used as a dismissive or unwilling response}})
#: {{syn|ru|[[да так|да '''та́к''']]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[что|Что]] [[с]] [[тобо́й]]? — '''Так'''.|What's up with you? — '''Nothing'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1859|author=w:ru:Иван Тургенев<t:{{w|Ivan Turgenev}}>|title=w:ru:Дворянское гнездо|chapter=s:ru:[[Дворянское гнездо (Тургенев)/Глава 1|Глава I]]|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Constance Garnett|title2=s:en:[[A House of Gentlefolk/Chapter I|A House of Gentlefolk]]|location2=|publisher2=|year2=1917|page2=|pageurl2=|text=— О чём ты э́то? — спроси́ла она́ вдруг Ма́рью Дми́триевну. — О чём вздыха́ешь, мать моя́?<br>— '''Так''', — промо́лвила та. — Каки́е чуде́сные облака́!<br>— Так тебе́ их жа́лко, что́ ли?|t="What's the matter with you?" she asked Marya Dmitrievna suddenly. "What are you sighing about, pray?"<br>"'''Nothing'''," answered the latter. "What exquisite clouds!"<br>"You feel sorry for them, eh?"}}
# {{lb|ru|in the following construction}} {{n-g|Used to express that something is what should be or happen.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[делать|Де́лать]] '''так''' [[де́лать]].|If we have to do it, then we should do it.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[мне|Мне]] [[всё равно́]]: [[щи]] '''так''' [[щи]], [[ка́ша]] '''так''' [[ка́ша]].|I don't mind: if it's [[shchi#English|shchi]], it's gonna be shchi, if it's porridge, let it be porridge.}}
# [[yes]], [[indeed]]
#: {{syn|ru|да|действи́тельно}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|when repeated}} [[well, well]]([[well, well, well|, well]])
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Так''', '''так'''(, '''так'''), [[вы]] - [[челове́к]] [[сло́ва]].|'''Well''', '''well'''(, '''well'''), you're a man of your word.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|when repeated}} [[now, now]]; [[okay]], [[okay]]; [[alright]], [[alright]]
#: {{syn|ru|[[ла́дно]], [[ла́дно]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Так''', '''так''', [[дава́й]] [[не]] [[бу́дем]] [[выходи́ть из себя́]].|'''Now, now '''/ '''okay, okay''', let's not lose our temper.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|with numbers}} [[around]], [[about]] ({{n-g|used to express approximation}})
#: {{syn|ru|где́-то|о́коло|приблизи́тельно|приме́рно}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[от|От]] [[вокза́ла]] [[до]] [[до́ма]] [[киломе́тра]] '''так''' [[два]].|It's '''about''' two kilometres from the station to home.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[это|Э́то]] [[произошло́]] [[лет]] '''так''' [[де́сять]] [[тому́ наза́д]].|It happened '''around''' 10 years ago.}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|ru|conjunction}}

# [[so]] {{gl|therefore, thus}}
#: {{syn|ru|зна́чит|поэ́тому|так что|таки́м о́бразом}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[обещал|Обеща́л]], '''так''' [[сде́лай]].|You promised, '''so''' do it.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[but]] (often with a sense of obviousness)
#: {{syn|ru|но}}
#: {{ux|ru|— [[здесь|Здесь]] [[оно́]] [[означа́ет]] «[[возмуще́ние]]». – '''Так''' [[э́то]] [[не]] [[подхо́дит]] [[по]] [[конте́ксту]].|— Here it means "outrage". — '''But''' that doesn't fit with the context.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[поехал|Пое́хал]] [[бы]], '''так''' [[де́нег]] [[нет]].|I'd go, '''but''' I don't have the money.}}
# {{n-g|Used similarly to {{m|ru|то}} in the following constructions (see {{m|ru|то}}); no translation.}}
#: {{syn|ru|то<q:partial>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[что|Что]] [[каса́ется]] [[криптовалюта|криптовалю́т]], '''так''' [[у]] [[нас]] [[о́чень]] [[мно́го]] [[вариа́нтов]].|As regards cryptocurrency, we have a lot of options.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[всё|Всё]], [[что]] [[тебе́]] [[ну́жно]] [[сейча́с]], '''так''' [[э́то]] [[запо́мнить]] [[все]] [[э́ти]] [[значе́ния]].|All you need now is to remember all these meanings.}}

